This is 99% invisible. I'm Roman Mars. On May 3rd, 1978, construction workers in San Francisco were digging a foundation for a new building on San St. Street. Right next to the tallest skyscraper in the city, the Trans-America pyramid in the heart of the financial district. They were about 20 feet below street level when their shovels hit something totally unexpected. It was the hull of an old ship. That's reporter Emmett Fitzgerald. Archaeologists immediately came in and started scraping away all the dirt and mud.
这里是“99%隐形”播客。我是罗曼·马尔斯。1978年5月3日，旧金山的建筑工人在三街（San St. Street）为一个新建筑挖地基。这个地点就在旧金山最高摩天大楼——金融区中心的泛美金字塔大厦旁边。当时他们挖到低于街面约20英尺的地方，铲子突然碰到了完全意料之外的东西。那是一艘旧船的船体。说话的是记者埃米特·菲茨杰拉德。考古学家们立即赶到现场，开始清理上面的泥土。

